# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATA-LEAK GUARD for on-prem client image builds (context = repo root).
#
# The live SaaS database, uploads, env files and secrets must NEVER enter a
# build context — an image ships to client hardware. Matching uses Docker's
# last-match-wins rule, so the `!release/seed/grc_seed.db` exception below
# must stay AFTER the `**/*.db` exclusion it punches through. `!` exceptions
# work against file-glob exclusions; do not replace the globs with a parent-
# directory exclusion (e.g. `release/`) or the re-include will stop working.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# VCS / tooling
.git
.gitignore
.claude
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Databases — the LIVE grc_dev.db above all. Only the cleaned seed re-enters.
backend/grc_dev.db
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
!release/seed/grc_seed.db

# Customer files and local state
backend/uploads
backend/venv
backend/env
backend/logs
test-documents
*.pdf
**/*.pdf
*.xlsx
**/*.xlsx

# Env / secrets — every variant, everywhere
**/.env*

# Frontend / marketing — dist may be what production serves; marketing never ships
node_modules
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
marketing

# Vendor-only docs and previous release outputs (keep seed + pyarmor regfile)
DEPLOYMENT_PRIVATE.md
release/*.tar.gz
release/bundle-*
